  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Prolonged period of dry weather continues for \nthe remainder of the week with a large diurnal temperature \nrange. Chilly nights with lows in the 20s & 30s. Unseasonably \nmild afternoons with plenty of sunshine allowing highs to reach \nthe upper 50s to well into the 60s at times.\n\nAn upper level ridge of high pressure will remain in control of our \nweather for the remainder of the week. The result will be the \ncontinuation of a prolonged period of dry weather along with a large \ndiurnal temperature range. The NBM guidance appears not warm enough \nduring the afternoons and not cool enough at night with excellent \nradiational cooling conditions much of the time. Low temps will \nmainly be in the 20s and 30s. Highs will be in the middle to upper \n50s today and then mainly in the 60s for the remainder of the work \nweek. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for some rain sometime Sun into Mon if a \ncoastal low pressure system tracks close enough to the coast...but \nthat remains uncertain.\n\nA vigorous piece of southern stream energy that will emerge \nfrom the Gulf into early next week. While this system will be \nloaded in moisture...it remains to be seen if northern stream \nenergy can amplify the upper level flow enough to allow this \nsystem to track up the coast. Now some of the ensemble guidance\nshows this occurring which would bring the potential for a \nwidespread heavy rain event sometime Sun into Mon. \nHowever...other guidance indicates that this low escapes out to \nsea and we remain generally dry outside a few brief showers. We \nwill likely need a few more days to have a better idea...so not \nmuch more to say at this point.",
